{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-g4:000001:issue_created:sase-g4:8d238337c309033c1aa1b06bca9b09c3aa4c3389d73f1a8d9bbb752b4e8bbfe0","timestamp":"2026-08-06T13:05:13Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.ty","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-g4","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-g4","title":"Reject a malformed plan-header block at validation time instead of mid-launch","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-08-06T13:05:13Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.ty","updated_at":"2026-08-06T13:05:13Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"A plan whose provenance header block is malformed is rejected the first time anything validates it — `sase plan validate`, `sase plan propose`, and the tale/epic approval gate — with a diagnostic that names the offending section and its line, so an approved epic can never reach `sase bead work` and abort at its archive step; and if the archive boundary is ever reached with a malformed document anyway, it fails with that same actionable diagnostic instead of a bare `validation:` exception from the Rust binding.","notes":"","design":"plans:202608/plan_header_validation.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","dependencies":[]}}}
